Component anatomy, class strings, and behavior contracts are ported from
these projects. No source code is redistributed verbatim; generated Elixir
modules are derived works produced by the pipeline in tools/.

Where an upstream component uses a JavaScript library, live_ai_elements uses
the Elixir library that does the same job rather than porting it. Each is an
optional dependency, so an application that wants none pulls in none:

  phoenix_streamdown — https://github.com/dannote/phoenix_streamdown
  Streaming markdown for LiveView, in place of AI Elements' use of Streamdown.

The codegen pipeline in tools/ reads upstream TypeScript with:

  oxc — https://oxc.rs
  Copyright (c) Boshen and oxc contributors, licensed under the MIT License.

It is a maintainer-only build dependency. Nothing it produces is redistributed,
and neither published package depends on it.
